  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThis plan introduces a novel spectral project-difference method for minimizing the Erd\u0151s minimum overlap constant. Unlike the previous optimization-focused approach, we use a coordinate transformation that decomposes the function representation into orthogonal basis vectors defined by difference sets. This leverages the underlying structure of the shift operation to create functions with low correlation at all shifts. Central to this is the mathematical insight that periodicity constraints combined with difference-set properties can systematically reduce maximum overlap. We replace gradient-based optimization with a greedy spectral projection that maintains feasibility and monotonically improves the objective. The key innovations are: (a) explicit modeling of shift-invariance via difference sets, (b) spectral projection dynamic programming and (c) analytic violation recovery for orthogonality constraints.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nVariables: h(x) \u2208 [0,1] with \u222b\u2080\u00b2 h(x)dx =1\nRepresentation: h(x) = 1/2 * (1 + \u03a3 a_m B_m(x)), where B_m are Bernoulli basis functions\nConstraints:\n- Non-negativity: a_m \u2265 -1\n- Non-overflow: \u2211|a_m|\u00b2 \u2264 (1+8/\u03c0\u00b2) (empirically derived)\n- Integral constraint enforced via pseudoinverse projection\n\nObjective: min max_k \u222b\u2080\u00b2 h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx\n\nImplementation:\nRepresent h on N=512 grid points for FAISS-accelerated correlation computation\nDefine penalty term: (1/2) \u2211_k |\u27e8h,h_{shifted}\u27e9 - 0.5|\u00b2\nUse ADMM to enforce orthogonality in K=16 singular values\n\n3. Implementation procedure\nParent validation:\n- Check current_best_n = 310\n- Prepare function for spectral basis: build_bernoulli_basis(310)\n- Execute standard repair: repair(h, n) with clipping and normalization\n\nCoordinate ascent:\n- Initialize walk matrix W from HxH correlation matrix\n- Apply spectral decomposition: eigens={energy[i]:vec[i] for i in sorted_args}\n- For top k singular vectors, compute violation = |\u27e8h,vec\u27e9 - C_max|\n- Projected gradient:\n    h_next = \u03a0 [h0 - \u03b3 * \u2207L(h)]\n    where L(h) = max_k compute_overlap(h,k)\n\nRegularization loop:\n- Energy Balancer:\n    for t in 20..budget_s by 1:\n        extract_top_moments_of(h)\n        repair h to satisfy constraints\n        update overlap at grid points\n        if n_iter % 100 == 0 and \u2207L(h).norm < 0.00001: rand_retrain(10)\n- CorrelationMonitor:\n    if c5 > best_c5*1.01: \u03bc,\u03c3 = mean_covariance(h, k_range=30)\n    for shift in sorted_top_shifts:\n        compute_exact_overlap(shift) using FAISS\n\n4. Search choices\n- Initial steps: 100 grid points (fast compute)\n- Transition factor: (best_c5/initial_c5) \u2248 0.38/0.5\n- Momentum decay: 0.95/step\n- Dimensionality reduction schedule:\n    D(t) = ceil(sqrt(N/t)) for t in [1, budget_s]\n    N base = 512, scale = 400, target precision = 0.3808\n\n5. Budget and robustness\n- Wall time: 1100s\n- Hardware: 1 CPU\n- Memory profile: \n    - Expand grid: O(N\u00b2) operations but FAISS handles with O(N log N)\n    - Early termination: if no 10-step improvement\n- Violation handling:\n    \u03b4 = valid_overlap - current_overlap\n    double \u03b4 is exponential decay factor, implemented as\n    decay = 0.38*dt/dt_prev if improvement otherwise\n    if n_violations>10: recurrent_violation_coeff *= 0.8\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n- Final candidate: \n    feasible = (h in [0,1] and sum(h)*dx =1)\n    overlap = exactly max(correlation)*dx with compute_overlap()\n    must have finite and non-NaN values\n- Must be representable in final 500-step computation\n- Restart signal: if c5 not improving for 100 steps\n- Output: (h_values, c5_bound, n_points)\n- Guarantee: the plan maintains an initial feasible vector throughout iterations\n\nExecution summary:\n- Use spectral projection to achieve C < 0.380894\n- Computation budget: 1100s\n- Termination condition: 1500-step plateau or explicit violation recovery\n- Primary innovation: coordinate descent with spectral basis projection",
